			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform plugin\n\nUpdate Cocoon and Output submodules to include the new ESBuild transform plugin that exposes VS Code's IInstantiationService and IWorkbench facade on globalThis. This enables Sky-side bridge code to resolve internal services (IStatusbarService, ISCMService, ICommandService, etc.) via __CEL_INSTANTIATION_SERVICE.invokeFunction() without re-implementing a parallel UI surface.\n\nThe transform patches web.main.js to stash the IInstantiationService after workbench.startup() and web.factory.js to expose the IWorkbench facade after workbenchPromise.complete(). Both injections are idempotent (short-circuit on existing marker) so re-running the transform on an already-patched tree is a no-op.\n\nImpact: Sky can now access VS Code's internal services directly, enabling proper integration of extension-contributed UI elements like status bar items and SCM providers.",
			"SHA": "f577e14dde8645c746c774043a104d37847326ad"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T01:22:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add workspace folders to extension host init, remove fallback status bar\n\nCoordinate init data and UI updates across Mountain and Sky submodules:\n\n- **Mountain (e10a5c04):** Add `folders` array inline to WorkspaceDTO in InitData so extensions reading `vscode.workspace.workspaceFolders` synchronously (vscode.git, eamodio.gitlens, typescript) see real folders immediately instead of `[]`. Also add `configuration` field for workspace config path. Enable CWD-autoload by default in debug builds (OFF in release) to support git repository scanning.\n\n- **Sky (05efccae):** Remove custom fallback status bar that was overlaying VS Code's native `.statusbar`. Extension-contributed status bar items are now dropped until `MainThreadStatusBar.$setEntry` is properly wired into the workbench. Add SCM event bridge handlers that dispatch `cel:scm:*` CustomEvents when Mountain emits `sky://scm/{register,unregister,updateGroup}`.\n\n- **Cocoon:** Submodule pointer update.\n\nImpact: Extensions like vscode.git and gitlens now surface tree-views on cold boot in debug builds. SCM state events are properly routed to Sky-side consumers.",
			"SHA": "21ddbb2453f9fd6da04c91cc929d7104a695cbfd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T00:09:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Improve Mountain gRPC reliability, cleanup Output config, fix Sky status bar\n\nMultiple cross-cutting improvements:\n\n- **Mountain (26891b30):** Implement exponential backoff for Cocoon gRPC handshake (50ms initial, 2s ceiling, 20s budget) replacing fixed 1s retry. Healthy spawns now connect in ~400ms vs previous ~20s. Add child-exit detection during connection loop to fail fast with actionable diagnostics when Node exits early (unhandled exception, invalid module). Handle activation-race TOCTOU for `_typescript.configurePlugin` commands with early null return. Add pre-flight bundle probe to fail fast on missing Cocoon bundle.\n\n- **Output (51de686e):** Remove Configuration source directory (ESBuild configs, TypeScript configs, build plugins, polyfills) from Output element. Output should contain only final bundled JS artifacts consumed by Cocoon at runtime. Configuration files should be regenerated from source definitions during build.\n\n- **Sky (2ed0e226):** Strip VS Code codicon syntax (`$(name)`, `$(name~spin)`) from status bar text before rendering to prevent garbled \"weird emojis\" in fallback bar. Change status bar items to ALWAYS use dedicated fallback bar - never inject into VS Code's native `.statusbar` DOM to avoid visual conflicts between two rendering systems.\n\n- **Sky deps:** Bump @xterm/xterm (6.1.0-beta.199→202), vite (8.0.9→10), @astrojs/compiler-rs (0.1.8→9).",
			"SHA": "31cf2b5f1cfd8b55ab088cd252ed860aea02fed9"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1782917469526
}